State:
• Build: the harness ran build and tests at session start; I didn't re-run them. The binary reports v0.5.0 (ce73bbab) and answered a -p prompt correctly.
• Evolve runs: the last 4 finished runs all succeeded, with no reverts in the window.
• Releases: v0.5.0 shipped this morning. The release notes record that 48 models' prices disagree with models.dev's list (on #1012).

What the planner should know first:
• Line-cap traps: src/context.rs is 2,035 lines and has no exemption entry in tests/module_size.rs. About 15 more lines makes cargo test fatal, which reverts the whole task. src/format/mod.rs is 86 lines past its exemption entry, with about 14 lines to spare. Any task touching either file has to split it or update its entry in the same diff.
• #1214 is live: I ran the built binary on files that already existed. --output out.txt silently replaced a file containing keep me, and --save-session sess.json did the same, both exiting 0. It's cheap to fix with the same refusal and --force pattern that /save and /export got, and it's the strongest candidate.
• Other candidates: #1213 (/spawn -o "a b.md" splits the quoted path, so the task text gets the rest), #1210 (a dangerous command only mentioned inside a quoted argument of a non-print command, like git commit -m "kill -9 1 at $(date)", is still refused as if it ran), and the next slice of #1184 (moving config onto the toml crate; 14 hits of the old line-by-line reading remain).
• Waiting on the owner: my A/B question on #1202 (whether unreadable commands should ask even under --yes, -p and piped input) has had no reply for about 2.4 days. That's inside his usual reply time, so hold and don't ship option B. #1215 is a fix to scripts/evolve.sh, which I'm not allowed to edit, so it's a question for him, not a task.
• Where to point the self-driven slot: help and session work each took 4 of the last 8 self-driven diffs. Files no prediction has ever covered: src/prompt/turn_prefix.rs, src/grep_status.rs, src/tools_child_bash_tests.rs.

Research: I read Claude Code's changelog for 2.1.328–2.1.329 (Nov 19) and saved a comparison to yopedia.
• The trust dialog now says where a folder's hooks are declared. That lines up with #1188, where yoyo's trust is tied to the project path, not the file's contents.
• /code-review now stops when gh pr diff fails. yoyo already does this, so there's no gap.
• Claude Code no longer fires its after-tool hooks for calls that were refused before they ran. I didn't trace where yoyo's safety refusal sits relative to its hooks, so whether yoyo matches is unverified.

